; Levy spearman — the first real enemy.
;
; Same combat components as the player and the training dummy. What is new is
; everything below $StateMachine: five State nodes, one per behaviour, plus a
; NavigationAgent3D for pathing and a Perception node that owns "can I see you".
;
; The state tree in the editor IS the behaviour list. To read what this enemy
; can do, expand StateMachine; to change when it gives up chasing, open Chase.
;
; Ranges have to sit INSIDE the hitbox's real reach or it parks just out of
; range and swings at air forever:
;   Hitbox reach   2.0m from body centre + target radius 0.45 = 2.45m contact
;   Chase.attack_range     1.9  (close to here, then start swinging)
;   Attack.break_off_range 2.3  (drift past here and go back to chasing)
; The gap between them is hysteresis, so a target hovering on the boundary
; does not flip between Chase and Attack every frame.
[gd_scene load_steps=21 format=3]

